I'm not sure what you mean by "all the rest of us".  My
experience has also been that there is a great deal of variance,
and that games without some normally common object aren't that
rare.  And basic statistical analysis, I think, supports this:
for any one common object (e.g. scroll of identity), a game
without it is probably very rare, but given the number of
different objects, there's a pretty good probability that at
least one will be missing.  Like Janis, I've had games with no
shops except the one guaranteed in Minetown, with no scrolls of
enchant armor before the castle, etc.  If you pick out any one
special case, yes, it's rare.  But the probability that you will
encounter at least one in a game is actually fairly high.

